      t: "O(1)",
      s: "O(1)",
      tags: ['optimal', 'interview-pick', 'elegant'],
      idea: "A power of two in binary has exactly one set bit. n-1 flips that bit and all bits below it. So n & (n-1) === 0 only when n is a power of two. Also check n > 0.",
      walk: [
        "If n <= 0, return false (powers of two are positive).",
        "Compute n & (n-1): clears the lowest set bit of n.",
        "If result is 0, n had exactly one set bit → power of two.",
        "Example: 8 = 1000, 7 = 0111, 8&7 = 0000 → power of two."
      ],
      notes: "This is the fastest method, O(1) with a single bitwise operation. Classic interview bit trick.",
      code: `function isPowerOfTwo(n: number): boolean {
  return n > 0 && (n & (n - 1)) === 0;
}`,
